---
import Architecture from '../../layouts/Architecture.astro';
import Diagram from '../../components/arch/Diagram.astro';
import Box from '../../components/arch/Box.astro';
import Edge from '../../components/arch/Edge.astro';
import Group from '../../components/arch/Group.astro';
import Label from '../../components/arch/Label.astro';
import Legend from '../../components/arch/Legend.astro';

// Entry-point columns: 3 columns, 190 wide, 16 gap, after an 80 unit row-label gutter.
const cx = (c: number) => 92 + c * 206;
const CW = 190;
const rows = { name: 20, before: 100, side: 198, protect: 296, route: 394 };
---
<Architecture
  title="Skipping"
  subtitle="Slam, quicken, requestSkip, slamStop, protect, groups, the generation counter."
  eyebrow="Presses"
>
  <p>
    A skip is a button press that asks reels to land sooner. pixi-reels has two ways to do
    that and three public entry points that decide which reels a press frees. The modes are
    <code>'slam'</code> (put each freed reel on its result frame and land it in the same tick)
    and <code>'quicken'</code> (end the tease, cut the stop delay, but still play the spin-out
    and bounce). Which reels a press frees is the same in both modes: that part is decided by
    <code>_pressSkip</code> from reel groups and tease protection, never by the mode. All of it
    lives in <code>packages/pixi-reels/src/spin/SpinController.ts</code>; the types are in
    <code>packages/pixi-reels/src/config/types.ts</code>.
  </p>

  <Diagram height={492} caption="The three public entry points, row by row. Only skip() carries the once-per-round side effect; only requestSkip() may be called before the result; only slamStop() walks past tease protection. Every column ends in _slamTargets or _quicken.">
    <Label x={16} y={rows.before + 34} text={['before', 'setResult']} mono />
    <Label x={16} y={rows.side + 34} text={['side', 'effect']} mono />
    <Label x={16} y={rows.protect + 34} text={['tease', 'protect']} mono />
    <Label x={16} y={rows.route + 34} text={['routes', 'through']} mono />

    <Box x={cx(0)} y={rows.name} w={CW} h={60} title="skip(options?)" kind="primary" sub="ReelSet.skipSpin()" />
    <Box x={cx(1)} y={rows.name} w={CW} h={60} title="requestSkip(opts?)" kind="primary" sub="ReelSet.requestSkip()" />
    <Box x={cx(2)} y={rows.name} w={CW} h={60} title="slamStop(opts?)" kind="primary" sub="{ reels } or { except }" />

    <Box x={cx(0)} y={rows.before} w={CW} h={78} title="throws" mono={false} kind="muted" sub={['the round is not', 'decided yet']} />
    <Box x={cx(1)} y={rows.before} w={CW} h={78} title="queues" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['_skipPending, skip:queued,', 'fires inside setResult']} />
    <Box x={cx(2)} y={rows.before} w={CW} h={78} title="throws" mono={false} kind="muted" sub={['no result frame', 'to place']} />

    <Box x={cx(0)} y={rows.side} w={CW} h={78} title="once per round" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['standard: speed boost', 'cascade: auto-slam refills']} />
    <Box x={cx(1)} y={rows.side} w={CW} h={78} title="none" mono={false} kind="muted" sub={['presses with', 'withSideEffects = false']} />
    <Box x={cx(2)} y={rows.side} w={CW} h={78} title="none" mono={false} kind="muted" sub={['skipStage only', 'is touched']} />

    <Box x={cx(0)} y={rows.protect} w={CW} h={78} title="honoured" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['protected tease reels', 'stay up']} />
    <Box x={cx(1)} y={rows.protect} w={CW} h={78} title="honoured" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['sees protection set', 'before setResult']} />
    <Box x={cx(2)} y={rows.protect} w={CW} h={78} title="ignored" mono={false} kind="muted" sub={['also ignores', 'defaultSkipMode']} />

    <Box x={cx(0)} y={rows.route} w={CW} h={78} title="_pressSkip(true)" kind="subtle" sub={['carried across', 'expand() steps']} />
    <Box x={cx(1)} y={rows.route} w={CW} h={78} title="_pressSkip(false)" kind="subtle" sub={['skipStage waits', 'for the fire']} />
    <Box x={cx(2)} y={rows.route} w={CW} h={78} title="_slamWithStage" kind="subtle" sub={['no arg: stage 2, full slam', 'reels/except: partial']} />

    {[0, 1, 2].map((c) => (
      <>
        <Edge from={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.name + 60]} to={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.before]} arrow="none" style="dotted" />
        <Edge from={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.before + 78]} to={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.side]} arrow="none" style="dotted" />
        <Edge from={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.side + 78]} to={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.protect]} arrow="none" style="dotted" />
        <Edge from={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.protect + 78]} to={[cx(c) + CW / 2, rows.route]} />
      </>
    ))}
  </Diagram>

  <div class="not-prose my-8">
    <Legend items={[
      { kind: 'primary', label: 'public entry', note: 'what your game calls' },
      { kind: 'accent', label: 'has a consequence', note: 'a queue, a side effect, or an honoured protection' },
      { kind: 'muted', label: 'inert', note: 'throws or does nothing on that row' },
      { kind: 'subtle', label: 'internal method', note: 'where the press goes next' },
    ]} />
  </div>

  <p>
    A fourth path is internal. <code>abortSlam()</code> is what the abort signal, the
    timeout and the <code>phase-chain-threw</code> recovery use: it ignores protection and
    <code>defaultSkipMode</code>, has no side effect, lands whatever is showing
    (<code>haltDrive</code> plus <code>snapToGrid</code>, no result frame needed) and goes
    through <code>_slamTargets</code> with every reel, which bumps the generation. A full
    slam always bumps <code>_spinGeneration</code>; a partial slam adds reels to
    <code>_slammedReels</code> instead, then re-runs <code>_announceAllStartedIfReady()</code>
    and <code>_tryBeginStopSequence()</code> so the stop gate is not left closed by a reel
    that never reached its spin phase.
  </p>

  <h2>Modes and option types</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>SkipMode = 'slam' | 'quicken'</code>. The default is <code>defaultSkipMode</code> on the controller, which the builder's <code>skipMode(mode)</code> sets, else <code>'slam'</code>.</li>
    <li><code>SkipOptions = {'{ mode?, speed?, payload? }'}</code>. <code>speed</code> names a registered profile that a quicken finishes on: its <code>spinSpeed</code> drives the spin-out and its bounce settings drive the landing. An unknown name throws at the call. A slam ignores it. <code>payload</code> passes through untouched to <code>onSkip(ctx)</code>, the skip events and <code>SpinResult.skipContext</code>.</li>
    <li><code>SkipContext = {'{ mode, speed?, payload? }'}</code> is what every phase's <code>onSkip</code> receives. Engine slams use <code>{'{ mode: \'slam\' }'}</code>.</li>
    <li><code>SkipInfo = SkipContext &amp; {'{ reels: number[], partial: boolean }'}</code> is the payload of <code>skip:requested</code> and <code>skip:completed</code>.</li>
    <li><code>SlamOptions = {'{ reels? }'} | {'{ except? }'}</code>, not both. Out-of-range indices are ignored; held and already-landed reels are never slammed.</li>
    <li>There is no <code>requestHurry</code>. "Finish faster" is <code>requestSkip({'{ mode: \'quicken\' }'})</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Which reels a press frees</h2>
  <p>
    <code>_pressSkip(withSideEffects)</code> runs for <code>skip()</code>, for a queued
    <code>requestSkip()</code> when the result arrives, and for a carried press at the start of
    the next <code>expand()</code> step. It asks <code>_nextSlamGroup</code> for the set of reels
    to free, then hands that set to <code>_slamTargets</code> or <code>_quicken</code>.
  </p>

  <Diagram height={544} caption="_pressSkip asks _nextSlamGroup which reels a press frees. Groups win over protection; protection only matters while there is an effective hold; and once only tease reels are left, 'stepwise' releases them one by one while 'once' and 'always' free nothing.">
    <Box x={200} y={20} w={230} h={60} title="press" mono={false} kind="primary" sub="skip() or queued requestSkip()" />

    <Box x={200} y={130} w={230} h={60} title="reel groups set?" mono={false} sub="setReelGroups()" />
    <Box x={500} y={121} w={200} h={78} title="next unlanded group" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['non-teasing reels first,', 'then its tease reels']} />
    <Edge from={[315, 80]} to={[315, 130]} />
    <Edge from={[430, 160]} to={[500, 160]} label="yes" />

    <Box x={200} y={240} w={230} h={60} title="protected tease reels?" mono={false} sub="_protectedTeaseReels" />
    <Box x={500} y={231} w={200} h={78} title="full slam / quicken" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['every reel still up,', 'stage 2, side effect now']} />
    <Edge from={[315, 190]} to={[315, 240]} label="no" labelDx={36} />
    <Edge from={[430, 270]} to={[500, 270]} label="no" />

    <Box x={200} y={350} w={230} h={60} title="non-tease reels still up?" mono={false} />
    <Box x={500} y={341} w={200} h={78} title="all but protected" mono={false} kind="accent" sub={['stage 1, side effect', 'waits for the next press']} />
    <Edge from={[315, 300]} to={[315, 350]} label="yes" labelDx={40} />
    <Edge from={[430, 380]} to={[500, 380]} label="yes" />

    <Box x={200} y={460} w={230} h={60} title="only tease reels left" mono={false} kind="muted" sub="which protect mode?" />
    <Edge from={[315, 410]} to={[315, 460]} label="no" labelDx={36} />
    <Box x={20} y={451} w={130} h={78} title="'stepwise'" kind="accent" sub={['one tease reel', 'per press']} />
    <Box x={500} y={451} w={200} h={78} title="'once' / 'always'" kind="muted" sub={['empty group:', 'the press does nothing']} />
    <Edge from={[200, 490]} to={[150, 490]} />
    <Edge from={[430, 490]} to={[500, 490]} />
  </Diagram>

  <p>
    The protected set is empty when <code>protect</code> is false, when <code>'once'</code>
    is already spent, when the effective hold is 0 or less (read from the profile captured
    for this spin), or when every tease reel has landed. <code>skipStage</code> is 0 at the
    round boundary, 1 when a press leaves something spinning (the side effect waits), and
    2 when a press ends the round: side effect applied, group freed.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two details on top of the picture. A quicken press counts reels it already quickened as
    down, so the next press moves on to the next group. And when groups are set, a press
    releases only the next group that has not landed: a game with
    <code>[[0, 1], [2, 3], [4]]</code> needs three presses to land everything.
  </p>

  <h2>Slam versus quicken on a stop phase</h2>

  <Diagram height={358} caption="A slam on a stop phase that is in its spinOut step. The running step is cancelled (phase:step cancelled), the rest are dropped, and onSkip sets the final pose in the same tick.">
    <Group x={20} y={20} w={680} h={318} kind="tint" label="slam" note="forceComplete(ctx)" />
    {(['delay', 'spinOut', 'land', 'bounce'] as const).map((s, i) => (
      <Box x={44 + i * 162} y={60} w={146} h={44} title={s} kind={s === 'spinOut' ? 'accent' : 'ghost'} />
    ))}
    {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
      <Edge from={[44 + i * 162 + 146, 82]} to={[44 + (i + 1) * 162, 82]} arrow="none" style="dotted" />
    ))}
    <Edge from={[279, 104]} to={[279, 150]} kind="primary" />
    <Box x={160} y={150} w={400} h={78} title="StopPhase.onSkip" kind="primary" sub={['haltDrive, placeStrip(targetFrame),', 'container back to _baseY, snapToGrid']} />
    <Edge from={[360, 228]} to={[360, 270]} kind="primary" />
    <Box x={240} y={270} w={240} h={44} title="landed, same tick" mono={false} kind="accent" />
  </Diagram>

  <Diagram height={358} caption="A quicken on the same stop phase. Only the cut step, delay, is skipped or cut short; spinOut, land and bounce still play, optionally on another speed profile named in the press.">
    <Group x={20} y={20} w={680} h={318} kind="tint" label="quicken" note="phase.skip({ mode: 'quicken', speed? })" />
    <Box x={44} y={60} w={146} h={44} title="delay" kind="muted" />
    <Box x={206} y={60} w={146} h={44} title="spinOut" kind="accent" />
    <Box x={368} y={60} w={146} h={44} title="land" kind="accent" />
    <Box x={530} y={60} w={146} h={44} title="bounce" kind="accent" />
    {[0, 1, 2].map((i) => (
      <Edge from={[44 + i * 162 + 146, 82]} to={[44 + (i + 1) * 162, 82]} />
    ))}
    <Edge from={[279, 104]} to={[279, 150]} kind="primary" />
    <Box x={160} y={150} w={400} h={78} title="ctx.speed (optional)" kind="subtle" sub={['its spinSpeed drives the spin-out,', 'its bounce settings drive the landing']} />
    <Edge from={[360, 228]} to={[360, 270]} kind="primary" />
    <Box x={240} y={270} w={240} h={44} title="lands after the spin-out" mono={false} kind="accent" />
  </Diagram>

  <h3>_slamTargets</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Emits <code>skip:requested</code> with <code>{'{ mode, reels, partial }'}</code>.</li>
    <li>Partial: calls <code>forceComplete</code> on each target's active phase and adds it to <code>_slammedReels</code>. Full: <code>forceComplete</code> on every phase and <code>_spinGeneration++</code>.</li>
    <li>With a result: applies any pending MultiWays reshape, then per reel <code>placeSymbols(decorated[i])</code>, <code>notifySpinEnd</code>, <code>notifyLanded</code> (which raises <code>spin:reelLanding</code>) and <code>_markLanded</code>. Without a result (abort): <code>haltDrive</code>, <code>snapToGrid</code>, notify, mark.</li>
    <li>Emits <code>skip:completed</code>.</li>
    <li>After a partial slam it calls <code>_announceAllStartedIfReady()</code> and <code>_tryBeginStopSequence()</code> again. Without this, reels that had not reached their spin phase when the slam happened could leave the stop gate closed for good.</li>
  </ol>
  <h3>_quicken</h3>
  <p>
    Marks the targets in <code>_quickenedReels</code> and <code>_quickenCtx</code>, sets each
    reel's <code>referenceSpeed</code> from <code>ctx.speed</code> if one was named, records a
    batch, emits <code>skip:requested</code>, then calls <code>activePhase.skip(ctx)</code> on each
    target. A phase that is not quickenable keeps running, and the chain applies the quicken at
    its next decision point: the spin phase drops its minimum to 0, the tease reel's phase is
    created already quickened through <code>primeQuicken</code>, and the stop phase gets
    <code>delay: 0</code> and <code>preserveSpeed: false</code>. <code>skip:completed</code> for a
    quicken fires later, from <code>_markLanded</code>, when the batch's last reel lands. In
    cascade mode a quicken is turned into a slam with a one-time <code>quicken-cascade</code>
    warning, because the cascade phases' slam pose is their natural end.
  </p>

  <h2>The generation counter and partial slams</h2>
  <p>
    Every reel chain captures <code>_spinGeneration</code> when it starts and checks
    <code>_isStale(reelIndex, generation)</code> after every <code>await</code>: stale if the
    generation moved on, or if this reel is in <code>_slammedReels</code>. A full slam bumps the
    generation, which silently ends every chain. A partial slam cannot do that, because the
    other reels must keep spinning, so it marks only its targets in <code>_slammedReels</code>.
    The watchdog, the abort callbacks and <code>_runReelTask</code> check the generation too, so
    late errors from an older spin are dropped. After a partial slam <code>skipStage</code> is
    left alone unless the slammed set covers every reel still spinning
    (<code>_slamWithStage</code>).
  </p>

  <h2>Reel groups</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>setReelGroups(groups | null)</code>: every reel must appear exactly once, otherwise it throws. It throws if called after any reel has landed in the current round. Groups persist across spins.</li>
    <li>When stopping, a reel waits in <code>_awaitGroupTurn</code> until every earlier group has landed. Stop delays become <code>positionWithinGroup * stopDelay</code>.</li>
    <li>When skipping, a press releases the next group that has not landed, non-teasing reels first.</li>
    <li><code>onReelsAdded</code> appends the new reels as one trailing group; <code>onReelsRemoved</code> filters them out, clearing the groups if nothing is left.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Protect modes</h2>
  <div class="not-prose my-6">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-muted/60">
          <tr>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">protect</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">First press</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">Later presses</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['false (default)', 'full slam, stage 2', 'nothing left to press'],
            ["'once' (or true)", 'lands the non-tease reels, stage 1', 'protection is spent: the next press slams the tease reels and applies the side effect'],
            ["'stepwise'", 'lands the non-tease reels, stage 1', 'each press releases the next tease reel in tease order; stage 2 on the last'],
            ["'always'", 'lands the non-tease reels, stage 1', 'a press never ends a tease; stage stays at 1 until the round ends on its own'],
          ].map(([m, a, b]) => (
            <tr class="border-t border-border/60">
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-primary text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{m}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-xs text-foreground/80">{a}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-xs text-foreground/80">{b}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    <code>protect: true</code> is normalized to <code>'once'</code> inside
    <code>setAnticipation</code>; storing the raw boolean used to behave like <code>'always'</code>.
    Protection applies to <code>skip()</code> and <code>requestSkip()</code> only, never to
    <code>slamStop()</code>. It is inert when the effective hold is 0 or less, and the hold is
    read from the profile captured for this spin, not the live one: on TURBO without a
    <code>duration</code> override the 250 ms hold keeps it active, on SUPER_TURBO it does
    nothing. Because <code>'always'</code> never reaches stage 2, check <code>isSpinning</code>
    before reading <code>skipStage</code> to decide whether a round is over. The tease itself is
    described on the <a href="/architecture/anticipation/">anticipation page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Across rounds and expand steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The first press that ends a round applies <code>_applyRoundSideEffects</code>: in standard mode it boosts to the registered profile with the highest <code>spinSpeed</code> and emits <code>skip:boosted {'{ previous, current }'}</code>; in cascade mode it sets <code>_autoSlamRefills</code>, so every later <code>refill()</code> in that round slams at once (and each refill's <code>setResult</code> presses a slam with no side effects).</li>
    <li>The boost calls <code>SpeedManager.set</code> directly, so it emits <code>skip:boosted</code> but not <code>speed:changed</code>. The next <code>spin()</code> restores the previous profile unless <code>setSpeed()</code> was called in between (<code>notifyManualSpeedChange</code>); that restore is a plain <code>set()</code> too, so it emits neither.</li>
    <li>Between two <code>expand()</code> steps the press is carried: <code>carrySkip</code> stores it, emits <code>skip:queued</code>, and the next step's <code>spin()</code> (with <code>continueRound</code>) turns it into <code>_skipPending</code> without resetting <code>skipStage</code>.</li>
    <li>If a phase chain throws, <code>_runReelTask</code> slams and the spin resolves with <code>wasSkipped: true</code>. Abort and timeout go through <code>abortSlam()</code> and reject instead.</li>
    <li><code>nudge</code> lives on <code>ReelSet</code>, throws while a spin runs, and is untouched by any skip; <code>skipNudge()</code> is its own thing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Events a press emits</h2>
  <div class="not-prose my-6">
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card overflow-hidden">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-muted/60">
          <tr>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">Event</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">Payload</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground">When</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[
            ['skip:queued', 'SkipContext', 'requestSkip() before the result; carrySkip between expand steps'],
            ['skip:requested', 'SkipInfo { mode, speed?, payload?, reels, partial }', 'start of _slamTargets or _quicken'],
            ['skip:completed', 'SkipInfo', 'end of _slamTargets; for a quicken, from _markLanded when the batch\'s last reel lands'],
            ['skip:boosted', '{ previous, current }', 'the round-ending skip() in standard mode'],
            ['spin:reelLanding / spin:reelLanded', 'reelIndex, symbols', 'per slammed reel, in the same tick'],
          ].map(([e, p, w]) => (
            <tr class="border-t border-border/60">
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-primary text-xs">{e}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground">{p}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-xs text-foreground/80">{w}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Defaults</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>defaultSkipMode</code>: <code>'slam'</code> (controller and builder).</li>
    <li><code>protect</code>: <code>false</code>. <code>true</code> means <code>'once'</code>.</li>
    <li><code>skipStage</code>: 0 at every round boundary; <code>_autoSlamRefills</code>: false.</li>
    <li>A refill with every reel already landed still emits the skip events on the full-slam path; a partial slam with nothing to land emits nothing.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-4">
    <div class="text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-primary mb-1">Where this lives</div>
    <ul class="text-sm space-y-1 text-foreground/80">
      <li><code>packages/pixi-reels/src/spin/SpinController.ts</code>: skip, requestSkip, slamStop, abortSlam, _pressSkip, _nextSlamGroup, _protectedTeaseReels, _slamTargets, _quicken, _applyRoundSideEffects, setReelGroups</li>
      <li><code>packages/pixi-reels/src/spin/phases/ReelPhase.ts</code>: skip, forceComplete, primeQuicken, the cut-step runner</li>
      <li><code>packages/pixi-reels/src/config/types.ts</code>: SkipMode, SkipOptions, SkipContext, SlamOptions, AnticipationProtect</li>
      <li>Recipes: <a href="/recipes/skip/">skip</a>. Related: <a href="/architecture/anticipation/">anticipation</a>, <a href="/architecture/speed-profiles/">speed profiles</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Architecture>
